1. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:38: "A quiet microphone isn't mistaken for silence, and a hum isn't mistaken for speech." No code settles this. It is an absolute claim about the model's accuracy.

2. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:174: "Voice mode can miss a soft first word in a quiet recording" and :175 "Singing and voice-like instruments may read as speech" are model behaviour that the code does not establish.

3. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:177: "A voice panned hard to one side sounds quieter to the voice model." The code shows only a one-channel read (MediaImporter+Speech.swift speechReader). The loudness effect depends on Core Audio's downmix.

4. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md, The controls table: "a clip the mix turns down below it is quiet" should say at or below. SilenceDetector.swift:411 treats a clip as quiet unless g > limit, so a gain exactly at the threshold is quiet.

5. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:136: 'with less context a windowed answer can differ slightly from a whole-clip one'. The code does not settle this; it only proves the 2 s pad.

6. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:178: "In a reversed clip a cut edge can be off by up to 32 ms." The code doesn't support this figure. The mirror's only recorded cost is one extra bucket at an exactly aligned window end, and a 32 ms chunk grid applies to every c

7. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:172: "Up to a frame can remain." This is per edge, so up to a frame at each end of a cut.

8. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:121 says Transcribe is disabled 'for a file no clip plays'. A file no clip plays never gets a row. The string is reachable only if the file goes missing while the sheet is open (FillerDetector.swift:145-158, FillerSheetController

9. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:98 says on-Mac transcription doesn't report fillers 'reliably'. The app says it does not report them at all (FillerSheetController.swift:84-86).

10. docs/guide/cleanup-tools.md:161-163 says each false-start cut runs 'from the first cut word's start to the last cut word's end'. The assistant's prompt directs it to get_timeline_transcript and to cut from the first word's cut_start to the last word's cut_
----
1:1. docs/guide/canvas-and-layers.md:123 says to press C or double-click "a clip that is not text" to enter crop mode. A nest clip has no canvas box, so C beeps on it and a double-click finds nothing to hit.
43:22. docs/guide/canvas-and-layers.md:60-61 lists '← → ↑ ↓ (canvas focused)' as a 1-pixel nudge and '⇧ + arrow' as 10 pixels. Arrow keys never nudge. Arrow-key events should carry the numeric-pad and function flags (a standard AppKit fact, implied by the exception at app/Sources/EditorWindow.swift:
45:23. docs/guide/canvas-and-layers.md:114 says 'an arrow-key nudge' edits the selected action's end state. No such nudge reaches the canvas, for the same reason.
63:32. docs/guide/canvas-and-layers.md, Obscure, last paragraph: 'Regions ... follow the layer through every move, scale, rotation and crop.' A crop is the one edit that can shift a region. Regions are measured from the centre of the cropped rect (core/src/model_regions.rs:28-32, Compositor.metal ob
